-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regression tests: the missing-fact variants (section 6 of the brief)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- S2-U: staff count unknown -> enterprise size undetermined, not "no".
#ASSERT `T1 enterprise size` `S2-U` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `T1 enterprise size` `S2` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ... but T1 as a whole is still settled, because S2 is not an online platform.
#ASSERT `T1` `S2-U` EQUALS LIST `Not relevant: not an online platform`

-- S3-U: designation unknown -> threshold met, designation outcome still open.
#ASSERT `VLOP threshold met` (`S3-U`'s `average monthly active EU recipients`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `T2` `S3-U` EQUALS LIST `Threshold met, not designated`, `Designated, obligations not yet applicable`, `Designated, obligations applicable`

-- S3-D: designated (and notified) 2026-08-01 -> obligations from 2026-12-01.
#ASSERT `T2` `S3-D` EQUALS LIST `Designated, obligations not yet applicable`
#ASSERT `T2` `S3` EQUALS LIST `Designated, obligations applicable`

-- S1-U: significant-users judgement undetermined, target-market limb still settles it.
#ASSERT `T4` `S1-U` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `T4 limbs` `S1-U` EQUALS LIST `s.4(5)(b) UK is a target market`

-- S4: 2.5m UK users settles both OSA thresholds as "not met" despite unknown resharing.
#ASSERT (`T3` `S4`)'s `Category 1 threshold met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`T3` `S4`)'s `Category 2B threshold met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`T3` `S4`)'s `Category 1 on the register` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The base services
#ASSERT `T1` `S1-J` EQUALS LIST `Section 3 does not apply, except Art 24(3) (micro or small enterprise)`
#ASSERT `T5` `S2` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`T3` `S2`)'s `Category 2B threshold met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`T3` `S3`)'s `Category 1 threshold met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `T5` `S3-J` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Traces
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#EVALTRACE `T2` `S3-U`
#EVALTRACE `T1 enterprise size` `S2-U`
